   "source": [
    "# Data Preprocessing — v1.0\n",
    "\n",
    "## Summary\n",
    "Cleaned and merged the constructor finance and F1 business datasets, resolved a structural missing-data issue, checked for target leakage, and produced two ready-to-use modeling datasets for the team.\n",
    "\n",
    "## What's included\n",
    "\n",
    "**Missing values**\n",
    "- `cost_cap_limit_usd_m` had 104 missing values, all in pre-2021 rows (`in_cost_cap_era == 0`). Confirmed this is structural — no cost cap existed before 2021, so there was nothing to record — not a data quality issue. Filled with `0` as a sentinel, valid only in combination with `in_cost_cap_era`. Verified zero missing values in cap-era rows.\n",
    "- No other missing values found across the remaining four source files.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Merge**\n",
    "- Joined `constructor_finances.csv` with `f1_business.csv` on `season` (left join). Row count confirmed unchanged at 164 — no duplication from the join.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Leakage check**\n",
    "- `total_revenue_usd_m` (team-level) is arithmetically derived from `sponsorship_revenue_usd_m + prize_money_usd_m` for the same row — excluded from all model features, since it's derived directly from our regression target.\n",
    "- `total_revenue_usd_m_group` (from `f1_business.csv`) is a season-wide F1 business total, independent of any single team. Verified via `groupby(season).nunique() == 1` across all 17 seasons. Kept as a feature.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Encoding**\n",
    "- `in_cost_cap_era` and `is_constructors_champion` converted to integer flags.\n",
    "- `team_name` one-hot encoded (`drop_first=True`).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Outputs**\n",
    "- `regression_dataset.csv` — target: `prize_money_usd_m`\n",
    "- `classification_dataset.csv` — target: `is_constructors_champion`\n",
    "- Both share the same feature set; both targets are excluded from each other's feature columns to keep the two tasks independent.\n",
    "- 80/20 train/test split for both. Classification split is stratified on the target to preserve the ~10% champion ratio, given the class imbalance (17 champion-seasons out of 164 rows).\n",
    "\n",
    "## Notes\n",
    "- `total_revenue_usd_m` is still present in the full merged dataframe for EDA/statistical analysis — it's only excluded from the modeling feature set.\n",
    "- `sponsorship_revenue_usd_m` and `prize_money_usd_m` remain in the feature set even though they combine to form the excluded column — this is a deliberate choice, not an oversight, since they're independent inputs rather than derived from the target.\n",
    "- Full reasoning for both decisions above is documented here so you guys don't need to re-derive it."
   ]
  },
